      "statusChangeID": "67a3c32c4fb7d3232eb9668b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks very much for the additional info. It looks like this avatar is using a parent constraint to freeze the armature's head bone to a position in the world. Unfortunately, because of timing dependencies, we cannot restore the change that was added in version 2024.4.2 that previously allowed this approach to work.\n\nThis issue is caused by the engine moving your head bone back to where it should normally be before your constraint runs later in the frame. This means freezing the constraint causes it to capture the position of the head on the armature rather than the position the constraint would otherwise move the head to.\n\nSince this problem only affects constraints attached directly to an avatar's armature, you should be able to restore this functionality on your avatar by making these changes:\n\n1. Create a new game object outside your avatar's armature and add a parent constraint to it.\n\n2. On this new parent constraint, assign your avatar's hand as the source.\n\n3. Change the parent constraint on your head to use your new game object as a source.\n\n4. In your animator, update your Head In World toggle to freeze and unfreeze the constraint on your new game object rather than the constraint on your head. Your Head In Hand toggle can keep targeting the constraint on your head.\n\nWe may update our constraints documentation in the future to mention this incompatibility.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
